      "content": "For blocking electromagnetic waves, the effectiveness depends heavily on the specific frequency and the wave's polarization. Lead is a dense material good for blocking lower-frequency radiation, while conductive metal meshes like copper or aluminum are often used for shielding higher-frequency radio waves. You would typically need to construct a complete enclosure—a Faraday cage—to be effective, not just line the desk. Before construction, research the exact frequency of the \"suppression\" you are worried about to select the proper thickness and material density for your desired blocking range.",
